  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "Suppose \\(A,\\) \\(B,\\) and \\(C\\) are three numbers for which \\(1001C-2002A=4004\\) and \\(1001B+3003A=5005.\\) The average of the three numbers \\(A,\\) \\(B,\\) and \\(C\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(3\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(9\\)",
    "E": "not uniquely determined"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The average requires only the sum \\(A+B+C\\). Adding the given equations helps because the \\(A\\)-terms combine as \\(-2002A+3003A=1001A\\), matching the coefficients of \\(B\\) and \\(C\\). Thus\n\\[\n1001A+1001B+1001C=4004+5005=9009.\n\\]\nDividing by \\(1001\\) gives \\(A+B+C=9\\). Therefore the average is\n\\[\n\\frac{A+B+C}{3}=\\frac93=3.\n\\]\nEvery triple satisfying the equations has this same average, so the answer is \\(\\boxed{3}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
